# Pipeline Viewer Conventions

## StepOutput.json Well-Known Fields

**Invariant**: ∀ handler H: H returns well-known fields in StepOutput.json ⟹
viewer auto-renders without custom event emission.

| Field | Type | Viewer renders |
|---|---|---|
| `verdicts_by_model` | `{model: {claim_id: {v, r}}}` | Vote matrix |
| `verified_facts` | `[{statement_id, text}]` | Accepted claims + badge |
| `rejected_claims` | `[{statement_id, text}]` | Rejected claims + badge |
| `authority_verdicts` | `{claim_id: {verdict, domain}}` | Domain routing tab |
| `claims_for_general` | `[{statement_id}]` | General routing list |
| `verifier_pool` | `[model_alias]` | Pool header |
| `originator` | `model_alias` | Originator label |
| `stats` | `{total_claims, accepted, rejected}` | Summary stats |
| `answer_sentences` | `[str]` | Sentence highlighting |
| `compound_decomposition` | `{decomposed_count, ...}` | Compound breakdown |
| `tiebreaker_triggered` | `{borderline_claim_ids, ...}` | Tiebreaker panel |

## Auto-Computed Stats

If `verified_facts` ∧ `rejected_claims` present ∧ `stats` absent:

```python
stats = {
    "total_claims": len(verified_facts) + len(rejected_claims),
    "accepted": len(verified_facts),
    "rejected": len(rejected_claims),
}
```

